A||N||21||SKIDMARK||What's the SCOOP?||||5||
Z||000000||SKIDMARK||11-21-2001||12:38 AM||||Anyone have some info on these scoops? Where to get? What they cost? Any problems?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://pstr-m01.ygpweb.aol.com/data/00B/78/75/81/04/ZTQgksRqiUpN7Ac5HUkhOT-qdCA0ytvo00A0.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://pstr-m01.ygpweb.aol.com/data/001/1E/3A/3F/11/3duJX47G+UZK0xlCq9eKoOQXePhDOy5Y0180.jpg"> <BR>I saw a gold Fiero around here a couple of years ago that had similar scoops on it and it looked pretty good. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Smoooooth GT||11-21-2001||12:41 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SKIDMARK:<BR><B>Anyone have some info on these scoops? Where to get? What they cost? Any problems?<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://pstr-m01.ygpweb.aol.com/data/00B/78/75/81/04/ZTQgksRqiUpN7Ac5HUkhOT-qdCA0ytvo00A0.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://pstr-m01.ygpweb.aol.com/data/001/1E/3A/3F/11/3duJX47G+UZK0xlCq9eKoOQXePhDOy5Y0180.jpg">  <BR>I saw a gold Fiero around here a couple of years ago that had similar scoops on it and it looked pretty good.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>First thing... They actually make you engine run hotter... <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Smooooth_Yellow_sig_3.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/texas_1.gif">          <BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||11-21-2001||01:09 AM||||First, as mentioned above they cause the car to run hotter. Second, As far as I know they are no longer made. They were originally made by IRM and they called them "Fi-Air-O" scoops. Many have looked but few have found them.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero_24||11-21-2001||08:41 AM||||Yes they are still made, but very expensive because they are in London.  All the shipping adds up.  Go to <A HREF="http://www.fierofactory.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierofactory.com/</A> <BR>I was going to buy mine from them until I learned they do not help much.<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||3
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||11-21-2001||10:00 AM||||For anyone who doesn't understand why they make the engine run hotter... the vents next to the decklid were designed to let hot air <B>out</B> of the engine bay- not to bring it in!  If you added another scoop/vent to the decklid (with ample airflow) it might work out better.<P>The other thing I've seen them used for, is air induction for an intercooler- someone had an intercooled turbo and located the intercooler directly below the driver's side vent- effectively using the scoop to cool the system!||||reg||1
Z||000005||grinthock||11-21-2001||10:01 AM||||Seen them, they look kinda cheezy, Race-Tech used one on their turbo car to force cold air down onto the intercooler||||reg||1
Z||000006||TRiAD||11-21-2001||10:58 AM||||Went through the links on the "FieroFactory" website, and didn't see any individual parts, only full kits. <P>Anyone got a direct link for web-impaired people like me?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fiero_24||11-21-2001||01:00 PM||||There was no direct link.  They make them to order.  I had to call about 10 places before I came up with the Fiero Factory #.  They are really nice to talk to, I think it is a father & son business.<P>Craig||||reg||1
Z||000008||Shaun41178||11-21-2001||01:17 PM||||ok everyone has said they make your engine run hotter.  I do agree with that.  <P>However can anyone back up these statements with real world tests?  I am going to have to say no!<P>Has anyone taken a thermometer and had it installed in the engine bay before and after the scoops were installed to see just how much hotter it runs?  I am going to say that noone has with oh 99.9 percent confidence.  So I guess what I am saying is that I am kind of upset with everyone is saying that it will be hotter without actually testing it themselves or determining just "how much" hotter engine comp temps will be.<P>Those things pull in so much air at driving speeds that I bet it actually keeps the engine compartment cooler.  The air will find a way out the bottom which probably will affect the cars handling at higher speeds.<P>However at idle or parked traffic those scoops will limit how much heat can can out as compared to the stock setup.  That is where it will make it run hotter.  How much hotter?  Hell I have no idea.  But I do know that there is only one way to trully find out.<P>If you want them for more for form then function then I say get them.  I think it adds an aggressive look to the car.  People will be wondering what you have under that hood that needs all that cooling  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  yea they might be a bit pricey but hey I say go for it if you realy want them and don't care about some "potentially" extra engine compartment temps.  Just run a cooler thermostat or something.  Won't help with how hot the air is but will keep the engine cooler.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
Z||000009||SKIDMARK||11-21-2001||01:42 PM||||I was thinking of puting a 12 volt muffin fan in each one and a thermostat that moniters engine compartment temps. Like mentioned above, at driving speeds there shouldn't be any problems. Also, I have a 160 deg. thermostat and HD radiator so the engine will run cooler anyway. I thought blowing the air down and out would work better than bringing the hot air off the exhaust up through the engine compartment. Besides, I think they're unique and look pretty good. Don't see many of them.||||reg||1
Z||000010||GTFiero1||11-21-2001||02:04 PM||||if you install the mustang scoop on the decklid then the engine wont run hotter||||reg||1
Z||000011||Pyric||11-21-2001||06:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SKIDMARK:<BR><B>I was thinking of puting a 12 volt muffin fan in each one and a thermostat that moniters engine compartment temps. Like mentioned above, at driving speeds there shouldn't be any problems. Also, I have a 160 deg. thermostat and HD radiator so the engine will run cooler anyway. I thought blowing the air down and out would work better than bringing the hot air off the exhaust up through the engine compartment. Besides, I think they're unique and look pretty good. Don't see many of them.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Mmmmmmmmmm.... Muffin fans....<P>You get those out of an Easy-Bake Oven? <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">   <P>Just kidding  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>"Never offend people with style when you can offend them with substance." <BR>--Sam Brown||||reg||1
Z||000012||banditbalz||11-21-2001||07:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>someone had an intercooled turbo and located the intercooler directly below the driver's side vent- effectively using the scoop to cool the system!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/racetechc_1.jpg"> <P>As Grinthock noted, this is Mireamme's turbo/intercooled 3.1 from the Fiero Shop in Toronto. She runs 13.4 in the quarter. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||banditbalz||11-21-2001||07:41 PM||||ooops, just noticed that pick doesn't show the scoop. Actually, I don't have any recent pics with the scoop. Sorry guys, but here is another pic of Mireamme's turbo walking away from my GT.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MeVsDevilish.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Formula88||11-21-2001||07:58 PM||||I don't really care for those, but I have seen on a Fiero around here similar scoops, but instead of going from the vent up over top of the roof, they go from the vent up and around to side of the sail panel.  They don't work on fastbacks, but on notchbacks, it puts the intake to the scoop right behind where the sail panel stops.  Actually looked like something the factory could have done.<P>As for cooling, you have to make changes to compensate.  Maybe it won't get a lot hotter, but the engine compartment in the Fiero is too hot to begin with.  I'd duct the scoops to put air where I want it, and vent the decklid inbetween (Mustang scoop, or if I did it, a center vent similar to Skitime's.)  It could work well for cold air induction and an oil cooler, or an intercooler, etc.  But I wouldn't just have them dump air into the engine compartment.  To me, that would be a waste of time.  ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Oreif||11-21-2001||08:02 PM||||The one's that wrap around the sails of a notchback are the "Lazy 'C'" scoops from FOCOA. I think they are the only ones who make those.||||reg||1
