Z||000021||qwikgta||11-23-2001||11:47 PM||||I have never measured the temp in my engine bay but I have to go with what GM wrote about the vents in the Fiero.  Basically the idea is that air travels under the fiero and is "sucked" into the engine bay from underneath the car.  The air escapes out through the vents on the deck.  I believe it is a pressure thing.  If you cut off the exit for the air to go you will increase engine heat.  So I believe that you need the vents on the deck.  I have added a Mustang scoop to the deck on my car, and I have not noticed any diff in the engine temp, it just looks cool and I like it.  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pic6_2.jpg"> <P>Rob<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_Pic_copy.jpg"> ||||reg||1
